mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — TikTok scripts\n\nWorked scripts as production docs (shot · on-screen text · spoken · sound · timing), with a\n1-second hook, a loop, and TikTok-search keywords — plus a \"polished ad\" version for contrast. Voice\nis the blunt indie-founder voice from earlier skills (short, dry, no exclamation marks, concrete).\nYour output uses the loaded `voice.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Example 1 — Storytime / talking head (filmed) · ~30s · goal: reach + saves\n\n**Concept:** we deleted our most-requested feature; the boring button won.\n**Sound:** original audio (your voice). **Format:** talking head, handheld.\n\n| Time | Shot | On-screen text | Spoken |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0:00–0:02 | Close, mid-sentence, looking at camera | **\"We deleted our #1 requested feature.\"** | \"We spent six months on the feature everyone asked for. Then we deleted it.\" |\n| 0:02–0:10 | Same, quick cut | \"nobody used it\" | \"Every sales call, people begged for it. We shipped it. Nobody touched it.\" |\n| 0:10–0:20 | Slight push-in | \"the boring button won\" | \"What they actually used was a tiny export button we kept ignoring. Built it in two days. Most-used thing we have.\" |\n| 0:20–0:28 | Cut, direct | \"watch what they DO\" | \"People tell you what sounds good and do something else. So now we watch behavior, not surveys.\" |\n| 0:28–0:30 | Back to opener framing | \"so we deleted it.\" | \"Which is how we ended up deleting our most-requested feature.\" ← loops to 0:00 |\n\n**Loop:** the last line flows back into the first frame — it replays seamlessly.\n**TikTok SEO:** \"feature\", \"SaaS product\", \"build\" spoken + on-screen; caption: \"How we decide what\nto build for our SaaS — behavior over requests.\" Keyword + niche hashtags (#buildinpublic #saas\n#productmanagement), not generic ones.\n**Caption + hashtags → `caption-writer`. Schedule → `scheduling-and-queue`.**\n\n---\n\n## Example 2 — Faceless listicle (AI b-roll + voiceover) · ~20s · goal: reach + saves\n\n**Concept:** 3 tools that replaced a $200/mo stack. **Format:** faceless, voiceover over b-roll.\n**Sound:** trending upbeat sound, cuts synced to the beat.\n\n| Time | Shot (Veo b-roll) | On-screen text | Voiceover |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0:00–0:02 | Fast push-in on a cluttered dashboard | **\"3 tools that killed my $200/mo stack\"** | \"Three tools that replaced two hundred dollars a month.\" |\n| 0:02–0:08 | Tool 1 in use | \"1. ___ (free)\" | \"One — handles all my scheduling. Free tier covers it.\" |\n| 0:08–0:13 | Tool 2 | \"2. ___\" | \"Two — does what I paid fifty bucks for.\" |\n| 0:13–0:18 | Tool 3 | \"3. ___ (the sleeper)\" | \"Three — the one nobody talks about. Wait for this one.\" ← open loop paid off |\n| 0:18–0:20 | Back to first frame | \"save this 👇\" | \"Save it before you renew anything.\" |\n\n**Loop:** \"save this\" + the fast pace invites a rewatch to catch all three.\n**Veo note:** b-roll only; per `veo-prompt-pack.md`, this is a fair AI use (faceless, cutaways) —\nbut a founder review to camera might out-trust it. **AI-disclosure auto on TikTok.**\n\n---\n\n## Contrast — the \"polished ad\" version (do NOT do this)\n\n- 0:00 a 2-second animated logo sting.\n- A voiceover in brand-announcer tone: \"At [Company], we believe…\".\n- Glossy, color-graded, no face, tagline card at the end.\n\n→ Reads as an ad in the first second; scrolled. On TikTok, the handheld founder-to-camera version\nbeats it every time. If a user asks for the ad version, redirect to native.\n\n---\n\n## What the good examples share\n\n- A **1-second hook** on all three channels (verbal + on-screen text + visual).\n- **Fast pace, no intro tax, no dead air.**\n- A **loop / rewatch trigger** built into the ending.\n- A **sound choice** named (original vs trending) and, when relevant, beat-synced.\n- **TikTok-search keywords** in spoken + on-screen + caption.\n- Native, not ad-like; on-voice; AI-disclosure where generated.\n"
